#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""puzzles.py: practice puzzles of the 19 puzzle kinds, generated by code with their exact answers.

  python puzzles.py --per-task 100 --seed 0 --out PZ.jsonl [--fingerprints toolkit|FILE] [--exclude PZ.jsonl ...] [--prefix pz]

One item per line: {id, source: "pz", subject: <kind>, task: "exact", problem, answer}: the toolkit's item form for an
exact-answer problem (prompt "...Think step by step, then give the final answer within \\boxed{}.", graded by the
boxed text after normalisation). Every puzzle is made here from names, numbers and word lists in this file; none is
taken from a question set. --fingerprints: "toolkit" (the question fingerprints the toolkit ships,
wsp.data.bench_fingerprints) or a file with one fingerprint per line: a generated puzzle whose fingerprint is in it
is dropped. --exclude: puzzle files made earlier; a puzzle that is also in one of them is dropped (so that puzzles
kept for a reading are never among those a fit sees).

Kinds: boolean_expressions, date_understanding, formal_fallacies, geometric_shapes, hyperbaton,
logical_deduction_{three,five,seven}_objects, multistep_arithmetic_two, navigate, object_counting, penguins_in_a_table,
reasoning_about_colored_objects, temporal_sequences, tracking_shuffled_objects_{three,five,seven}_objects, web_of_lies,
word_sorting.
"""
